   $q$Which theme do both texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Young people rarely respect the work done by those who came before them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Travel to faraway places is the only real way to make important discoveries.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Knowledge grows when people admit what they do not know and leave room for others.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The most skilled experts should keep their discoveries private to protect their fame.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Knowledge grows when people admit what they do not know and leave room for others.$q$, $q$Tamsin says "I ran out of knowing," and the old log asks "Somebody please find out why," and in both cases later people add to the record. Hiroshi works from a school rooftop, so travel is not essential to the shared theme.$q$, 'draft', '849e954b-34f1-59da-bde2-c7abf33fda03')
