   $q$Which statement best explains how Text 2 transforms the folk tale's ending?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both endings show the characters punished for laziness, with no chance to make up for their mistakes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"Brannoch relearns his skill alone over a week, but the club recovers in one night by working together and then records what they learned.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Brannoch never repairs his mill and leaves town, but the club fixes the script easily and goes home early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Both endings show that hand methods are always faster than machines, even for large jobs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Brannoch relearns his skill alone over a week, but the club recovers in one night by working together and then records what they learned.$q$, $q$Text 1 ends with the miller grinding beside his neighbor for a week, while Text 2 compresses recovery into one night of teamwork plus written instructions. Both characters do recover, so the punishment reading ignores the hopeful endings.$q$, 'draft', '3b455230-0936-58e9-b7bb-34dc54865426')
