   $q$Why might the author of Text 2 have kept Mateo out of sight at the end, instead of moving him to the front as Text 1 does with Suri?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To suggest that some roles matter precisely because they stay hidden, so recognition need not mean a change of place.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To suggest that Mateo wanted to become an actor but was too shy to try out for a role.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To suggest that the director was unfair to Mateo and refused to thank him in public.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"To suggest that Mateo did not truly help the show, since the actors fixed the problem by themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To suggest that some roles matter precisely because they stay hidden, so recognition need not mean a change of place.$q$, $q$Mateo "had not wanted applause" and his calm cues work only from the dark, so the story honors him without moving him. The director does thank him publicly, so the unfairness choice contradicts the text.$q$, 'draft', 'cc3fe6f9-1c9a-5c29-801d-7ab56ebf3685')
