   $q$In paragraph 3, the water levels "equalize." Based on the context, "equalize" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"drain completely out of the lock","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"become the same as each other","is_correct":true},{"text":"flow faster through the valves","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"push the boat toward the gate","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$become the same as each other$q$, $q$The levels equalize when the water inside "reaches the same height as the water beyond the upper gate," so the word means become the same. The text says the boat rises with the water, but that is a result, not the meaning of equalize.$q$, 'draft', 'fcbdb092-21f2-56a5-bc50-13f4d8433832')
