   $q$In paragraph 1, Biscuit is described as "timid." What does "timid" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"shy and easily frightened","is_correct":true},{"text":"sick and needing rest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"hungry and in need of food","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"playful and full of energy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$shy and easily frightened$q$, $q$The examples that follow, "flinching at every slammed door and hiding in the back corner," show that timid means shy and easily scared. Nothing in the paragraph suggests Biscuit is playful or energetic.$q$, 'draft', 'a0a4e800-e549-54e4-8287-9f85885ad87b')
