   $q$In paragraph 3, Kwame tries to "coax" Biscuit forward. Based on what he does, "coax" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"to gently persuade someone to do something","is_correct":true},{"text":"to feed an animal at a set time","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"to train a dog to obey commands","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"to force someone to move by pulling","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to gently persuade someone to do something$q$, $q$Kwame "did not pull on a leash or raise his voice" but used treats and soft words until Biscuit came to him, so coax means to persuade gently. Pulling on a leash is exactly what the text says he avoided.$q$, 'draft', 'a0a4e800-e549-54e4-8287-9f85885ad87b')
