  ('12062ff4-23ee-5e99-baca-836dd5e5f1ba', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In paragraph 5, the manager says Biscuit "has turned a corner." What does this phrase mean in context?$q$, $q$[{"text":"has begun to improve after a difficult time","is_correct":true},{"text":"has become too attached to one volunteer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"has walked to a new part of the shelter","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"has started to behave worse than before","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$has begun to improve after a difficult time$q$, $q$Biscuit now trots to the front of her kennel and leans against Kwame, and soon after she is adopted, so the phrase means she has started to get better. Reading it as walking to a new place takes the figurative phrase literally.$q$, 'draft', 'a0a4e800-e549-54e4-8287-9f85885ad87b')
