values
  ('a2ef93a4-6369-5973-805b-e1022f3d3ce0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Ngozi calls the serve "awfully good," and Amara says there was "no higher praise." What is the effect of this oxymoron?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the sisters disagree about whether the serve was legal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Ngozi is criticizing the serve for being too risky.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It shows that Ngozi secretly thought the serve was a lucky mistake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It pairs a negative word with a positive one to make the praise stronger.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It pairs a negative word with a positive one to make the praise stronger.$q$, $q$Here "awfully" works as an intensifier, so the contradiction of "awful" and "good" makes the compliment playful and emphatic, which is why Amara calls it the highest praise. Reading "awfully" literally as criticism ignores Amara's happy reaction.$q$, 'draft', 'b3d29201-729c-5bf3-ad92-e68fe982d3cb')
