   $q$The author says a jacket labeled "ready for a new adventure" is not really making plans. What kind of language is this label?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A literal description of where the jacket will travel next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"A warning that the jacket is too worn out to be useful.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"An oxymoron that joins two words with opposite meanings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-device"},{"text":"A euphemism that turns attention from the jacket's past to its future.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A euphemism that turns attention from the jacket's past to its future.$q$, $q$The passage lists it among "clear euphemisms" and says it "asks the buyer to think about the future instead of the past." The phrase contains no pair of opposite words, so it is not an oxymoron.$q$, 'draft', 'c715a5ec-fabf-5e3c-b191-c6859aba3332')
