   $q$How does the connotation of "gently worn" differ from the connotation of "used"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Gently worn\" suggests a cheaper price than \"used\" does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"\"Gently worn\" suggests careful treatment, while \"used\" can suggest wear.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Gently worn\" suggests the item is newer than a \"used\" one is.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"\"Gently worn\" sounds more businesslike and neutral than \"used.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-terms"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Gently worn" suggests careful treatment, while "used" can suggest wear.$q$, $q$The author says "gently worn" invites shoppers "to imagine a careful former owner," while "used" can suggest something "tired, dirty, or close to the end of its life." The passage calls "previously owned," not "gently worn," the neutral and businesslike phrase.$q$, 'draft', 'c715a5ec-fabf-5e3c-b191-c6859aba3332')
