   $q$Why does the author say "None of these words is a lie" near the end of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To show that the labels differ in feeling, not in factual meaning.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To claim that \"full of character\" means an item has no flaws.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"To prove that shoppers are always tricked by secondhand labels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"To argue that sellers should stop using any word except \"used.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To show that the labels differ in feeling, not in factual meaning.$q$, $q$The author's point is that the labels share a denotation but create different feelings, so readers should "separate the facts about an item from the feelings the label is trying to create." The author never tells sellers to stop using these phrases.$q$, 'draft', 'c715a5ec-fabf-5e3c-b191-c6859aba3332')
