  ('9316759d-d749-5832-b032-1930e6052531', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The author says the octopus's skin "works like a living screen." What does this simile mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The skin can show changing colors and patterns very quickly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The octopus's skin blocks light the way a window screen does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-meaning-of-word"},{"text":"The octopus can watch shows and pictures on its own body.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The skin is hard and flat, like the glass on a device.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The skin can show changing colors and patterns very quickly.$q$, $q$The simile follows the explanation that the octopus changes "patterns in less than a second," just as a screen changes images. The passage stresses the octopus's soft body, so the skin is not hard like glass.$q$, 'draft', '722083c6-6b19-5207-9ec3-f9fcc6af7d55')
