   $q$The author calls the octopus "the ocean's quick-change artist" in the title. What does this phrase suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The octopus changes its appearance quickly and with great skill.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The octopus performs for scientists in exchange for food.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The octopus paints pictures on rocks along the sea floor.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The octopus moves from one ocean to another very quickly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The octopus changes its appearance quickly and with great skill.$q$, $q$A quick-change artist is a performer who switches costumes fast, which matches the octopus changing color and texture "in less than a second." The phrase describes appearance, not travel between oceans.$q$, 'draft', '722083c6-6b19-5207-9ec3-f9fcc6af7d55')
