  ('c16d3e0c-ed93-522f-8f02-c8cba129da29', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-figurative-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Scientists describe the octopus as "hiding in plain sight." Why does this phrase seem to contradict itself?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because scientists cannot agree on whether octopuses hide at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Because octopuses only hide at night, when nothing is in plain sight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Because the octopus swims away instead of hiding from predators.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Because \"hiding\" means being out of view, yet the octopus stays in the open.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because "hiding" means being out of view, yet the octopus stays in the open.$q$, $q$The passage explains that the animal "is right there in the open but does not register as an animal at all," so it is hidden while being fully visible. The passage describes camouflage, not swimming away.$q$, 'draft', '722083c6-6b19-5207-9ec3-f9fcc6af7d55')
