   $q$The author says "a strange fever swept through many cities." What does the word "fever" mean in this sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A sudden, intense excitement shared by a large number of people.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A period of hot weather that made people want to ride outside.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-target"},{"text":"A fear of bicycles that spread after several accidents.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"A sickness that caused many people to stay home from work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A sudden, intense excitement shared by a large number of people.$q$, $q$The next sentences say "It was not an illness. It was a passion for bicycles," so "fever" is a metaphor for widespread excitement. The author directly rules out the literal meaning of sickness.$q$, 'draft', '21297116-8a38-59cf-b06a-e1d983fd9485')
