   $q$Ms. Petrakis "appeared at the end of the aisle like a ship coming into harbor." What does this simile show about her?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She arrived late because she had to walk from far away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She was nervous and unsure about what to say next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"She was carrying a heavy load of boxes down the aisle.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She arrived in a calm, steady way that settled the situation.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She arrived in a calm, steady way that settled the situation.$q$, $q$The simile is followed by the words "calm and steady," and a ship entering harbor moves slowly and smoothly to a safe place. Her actions afterward (listening, nodding, offering help) show confidence, not nervousness.$q$, 'draft', 'd9955455-305e-502d-934b-7b6201903b64')
