   $q$At the end, Jun realizes "the cold period had been his own invention." What is the effect of this phrase?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that periods should never be used at the end of texts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"It shows that Marisol had invented an excuse to hide her anger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Jun had secretly typed the message himself as a joke.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that the unfriendly tone came from Jun's reading, not from Marisol's meaning.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that the unfriendly tone came from Jun's reading, not from Marisol's meaning.$q$, $q$Marisol says she "meant fine, like fine," so the coldness existed only in how Jun interpreted the punctuation; that is the "invention." Nothing suggests Marisol was lying, since she answered "laughing" and was "clearly confused."$q$, 'draft', 'c639ac32-73f1-5922-9044-9b583b0e2340')
