   $q$Which phrase signals that the story is moving back in time?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Last spring, at this same tournament\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Now she looked at the bishop again\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-return-with-shift"},{"text":"\"for the first time all afternoon\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-time-marker"},{"text":"\"Somewhere in the bleachers\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"place-not-time"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Last spring, at this same tournament"$q$, $q$"Last spring" moves the reader into a memory of an earlier game. "Now she looked" does the opposite: it brings the story back to the present.$q$, 'draft', 'ab4dabcd-6304-5dc8-a039-4a83aae55836')
