   $q$How does the author slow the pacing in the third paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By using very short sentences that count seconds, stretching a brief moment to build tension","is_correct":true},{"text":"By adding a long explanation of how a chess clock works","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"By switching the narration to Daniel's thoughts about the board","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-point-of-view"},{"text":"By jumping forward to the trophy ceremony and then returning to the game","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By using very short sentences that count seconds, stretching a brief moment to build tension$q$, $q$"One second. Two." and the exact clock time make a few seconds feel long, which builds tension. The story never jumps to a ceremony or enters Daniel's thoughts.$q$, 'draft', 'ab4dabcd-6304-5dc8-a039-4a83aae55836')
