   $q$Why does the story end with Priya breathing rather than with a statement of who won the game?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because the real turning point is Priya resisting the trap, so the story ends on her relief instead of the final score","is_correct":true},{"text":"Because the author ran out of time to describe the rest of the game in detail","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"outside-the-text"},{"text":"Because the flashback already revealed the winner of this year's game","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-flashback"},{"text":"Because the author wants readers to believe Priya lost again, just as she did last spring","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the real turning point is Priya resisting the trap, so the story ends on her relief instead of the final score$q$, $q$Daniel's smile and withdrawn hand show his plan has failed, so the tension that matters is resolved in Priya's breath. The flashback describes last year's game, not this one.$q$, 'draft', 'ab4dabcd-6304-5dc8-a039-4a83aae55836')
