   $q$How does the printed grade report change the tension in the scene?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It has no effect, because Linh's mother cannot read the comments.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It brings the tension to a peak, because numbers need no translation and Linh loses control of the message.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It ends the tension because the report shows Linh's grades are fine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It increases tension by making Mr. Halvorsen angry at Linh's mother.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It brings the tension to a peak, because numbers need no translation and Linh loses control of the message.$q$, $q$The mother "can read numbers," so the 52 reaches her without Linh as a go-between. Not reading the comments does not matter, because she finds the grade herself.$q$, 'draft', '878522c9-b6f8-5d26-9a4e-264b65f9fdcb')
