   $q$What is the effect of the final line, "This time, I use all the words"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It suggests that Linh will keep hiding her grades from her mother in the future.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It shifts the story into Mr. Halvorsen's point of view for the ending.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-point-of-view"},{"text":"It reveals that Linh never understood English well enough to translate the first time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It echoes the teacher counting words and shows Linh choosing honesty, closing the scene quietly instead of with an argument.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It echoes the teacher counting words and shows Linh choosing honesty, closing the scene quietly instead of with an argument.$q$, $q$Mr. Halvorsen noticed her answer "had fewer words than his," and the last line answers that by having Linh tell the full truth. She understood perfectly the first time; she chose what to leave out.$q$, 'draft', '878522c9-b6f8-5d26-9a4e-264b65f9fdcb')
