   $q$How does the final paragraph contribute to the development of the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It suggests that the town regrets giving up the pond harvest and hopes to bring it back.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It adds a new argument that museums are the best way to teach young people about history.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It shifts the focus to the invention of electric refrigerators and how they work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It explains why the harvest ended and shows that the practice is now remembered as part of the town's history.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains why the harvest ended and shows that the practice is now remembered as part of the town's history.$q$, $q$The final paragraph gives the reason the harvest stopped, affordable refrigerators and factory ice, and notes that the icehouse is now a museum. It never says the town wants the harvest back.$q$, 'draft', 'f8ffdc5d-ec43-5b96-b88d-2d24c3003147')
