  ('26200882-ce7a-5d7d-9e93-14b45e3a2e08', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-main-idea-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How does the third paragraph develop the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that most runners quickly give up on the negative split plan.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It describes the history of the negative split and who first invented it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It proves that watches are the most important tool a runner can own.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"It explains how the coach trains runners to learn and hold an even pace.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains how the coach trains runners to learn and hold an even pace.$q$, $q$Paragraph 3 begins "Learning this plan takes practice" and describes the watch checks and passing strategy. Runners find the pace frustrating "at first," but the passage says they learn it, not that they give up.$q$, 'draft', 'f8986b94-c83e-5075-9917-4d2b7cdc8c2d')
