   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The Kessler Gazette was the most widely read weekly newspaper in its region.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"outside-knowledge"},{"text":"Small towns should stop printing newspapers and publish only online.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A library saved a town's crumbling newspaper archive by scanning it, which made local history easy for everyone to use.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Old newspaper is made from cheap paper that turns yellow and brittle over time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A library saved a town's crumbling newspaper archive by scanning it, which made local history easy for everyone to use.$q$, $q$The passage moves from the danger to the old pages, to the scanning project, to its many uses, which the third choice sums up. The fact about cheap paper only explains why the pages were in danger.$q$, 'draft', '9d358747-3e82-5d3b-9a45-edf1c1c1ef15')
