   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Hand-painted signs nearly vanished but are returning in Port Alder because owners value them and new painters are learning the craft.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Printed vinyl signs are poorly made and should be banned from city streets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Every shop in Port Alder has now replaced its printed sign with a painted one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Ingrid Matsuda teaches evening classes at a community art center in Port Alder.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Hand-painted signs nearly vanished but are returning in Port Alder because owners value them and new painters are learning the craft.$q$, $q$The passage traces the decline of hand-painted signs and the two reasons for their return. The classes are one of those reasons, so the first choice is too narrow.$q$, 'draft', '039e26ac-b513-5abf-8a33-47a590660b5c')
