   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Salmon find their home streams mainly by watching for familiar rocks and plants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Dams are the only reason that salmon fail to return to their home streams.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Salmon spend several years traveling through the ocean before they lay eggs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Salmon likely find their birth streams by memorizing their scent, with other senses guiding them at sea, and this knowledge can help protect them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Salmon likely find their birth streams by memorizing their scent, with other senses guiding them at sea, and this knowledge can help protect them.$q$, $q$The passage explains the role of smell, the likely role of magnetism at sea, an experiment and why it matters. Rocks and plants matter only because they give each stream its scent, not because salmon see them.$q$, 'draft', 'a7518606-4d24-520b-9ca8-67e6ff0874ed')
