   $q$Which evidence best supports the inference that Bao was ready to run the board?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"He slid the board a few inches to the left.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"Bao handed her his granola bar.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"Bao said yes before he had time to be scared.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-evidence"},{"text":"\"Bao had memorized all of them by the second week of rehearsal.\"","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Bao had memorized all of them by the second week of rehearsal."$q$, $q$Knowing all sixty-three cues by heart shows he was prepared to run them. Saying yes quickly shows willingness, not that he had the knowledge to succeed.$q$, 'draft', '35c073ad-d385-59ff-94db-6d992a259a4d')
