   $q$Which statement best explains Nadia's response at the end, and is supported by the text?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She chooses to keep the visits going, as shown by bringing her own photo album the next week.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She is hurt by the trick and plans to stop visiting, as shown by her standing on the step.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She wants her Sundays back for soccer, as shown by her arriving early that day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She believes he forgot again after the call, as shown by her offer to start over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She chooses to keep the visits going, as shown by bringing her own photo album the next week.$q$, $q$Nadia plays along by "starting again" and then brings her own album, so she now wants the visits too. She saw him use the tablet easily, so she cannot believe he forgot, and she "did not mention soccer at all."$q$, 'draft', 'f4c42000-e62e-5d28-9ec4-66a595b9f8e0')
