   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tomas rebuilds a game at home and gets stuck at move fourteen, where a knight sits on the board's edge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Tomas loses to Lin, quits the chess club in frustration, and later becomes her coach at a big tournament.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"After a long winning streak, Tomas loses to a careful younger player, studies the game in a notebook, and returns to learn more from her.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Arrogant Tomas finally gets what he deserves when a clever sixth grader humiliates him at the club.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After a long winning streak, Tomas loses to a careful younger player, studies the game in a notebook, and returns to learn more from her.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers the streak, the loss, the notebook, and the rematch without judging Tomas. Calling him arrogant and saying he got what he deserved adds opinions that an objective summary leaves out.$q$, 'draft', 'c542e562-63e4-56f5-9fec-55eb5210faad')
