  ('c27a3d85-0080-5399-9e37-3d38338c1902', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker describes eggs on milkweed leaves turning into striped caterpillars and then into butterflies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The speaker describes a beautiful and amazing migration that everyone should travel to see at least once.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"The speaker describes butterflies whose migration takes several generations, none finishing the whole trip, and links this to starting work others will complete.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker follows one brave butterfly that flies from the mountains to the northern lakes and back again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker describes butterflies whose migration takes several generations, none finishing the whole trip, and links this to starting work others will complete.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers the generations, the unfinished journey, and the speaker's final reflection. The poem says "Not one has stood at both ends of the road," so a single butterfly making the whole trip is false.$q$, 'draft', 'cb146cb0-3216-53e1-887d-2b0f5e020adb')
