  ('a37daf18-5f3d-5cc8-b62d-3a39e9808ffd', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What role does the line "The journey is not theirs to finish" play in the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It tells the reader that the migration ends in the second stanza.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It shows that the speaker feels sorry for the butterflies and wants to help them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains that the first butterflies turn back because the trip is too hard.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It introduces the idea that each generation completes only part of the trip, which the poem builds on.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It introduces the idea that each generation completes only part of the trip, which the poem builds on.$q$, $q$After this line the poem follows daughters, granddaughters, and later generations, each flying one leg. Nothing says the first butterflies turn back; they lay eggs and "do not rise."$q$, 'draft', 'cb146cb0-3216-53e1-887d-2b0f5e020adb')
