  ('337dce6b-a92f-5c84-b09a-326aacd382ef', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g9-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A foolish fox wastes a whole summer on silly imitations before finally learning to be sensible.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Ashamed of her bark, a fox imitates other animals without success until her own bark warns deer of a flood, and she learns to value it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sorrel learns to hoot like an owl, and the owl tells her that her hoot is very close.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A fox imitates a wolf so well that the wolves invite her to join their pack for the winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ashamed of her bark, a fox imitates other animals without success until her own bark warns deer of a flood, and she learns to value it.$q$, $q$The correct summary covers her shame, her failed imitations, the flood, and her change. Calling her "foolish" and her efforts "silly" adds judgments that an objective summary avoids.$q$, 'draft', '8a38b6e1-9414-5766-8c8d-d57008b44844')
